Note: Testing functions, conditions, loops, collections, and phrases
Create a function called classify that accepts number n and gives back text,
    When n is greater than 10,
        return "Large".
    Otherwise when n is equal to 10,
        return "Ten".
    Otherwise,
        return "Small".

Create a variable called nums with value a list of 5, 10, and 20.
For every x in nums,
    Create a variable called cat with value call classify with x.
    Show x followed by ": " followed by cat.

Create a variable called first_val with value the first item of nums.
Show "First item is: " followed by first_val.

Create a variable called root with value square root of 64.
Show "Square root of 64 is " followed by root.
